          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can I use the security deposit as last month’s rent in NJ?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "No. NJ law explicitly prohibits using the security deposit as last month’s rent unless the tenant and landlord agree to it in writing at the time of termination. If last month’s rent is collected at move-in, it counts toward the 1.5x cap."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What if the tenant doesn’t provide a forwarding address?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "The 30-day clock may not start until you have a forwarding address. However, you should still make a good-faith effort to return the deposit. Document your attempts."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Does the security deposit limit apply to month-to-month tenancies?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. The 1.5x limit applies to all residential tenancies in New Jersey, regardless of term length."
